[recv] {"type": "message_start", "message": {"role": "toolResult", "toolCallId": "call_MEmaoPCEub2VYjSaczsRP0L8|fc_04b434c374dcd838016acd0c3e31a887d1816132c613ccad17", "toolName": "read", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "I’ve confirmed the worktree already contains generated metadata and a modified filter. I’ll preserve those changes, run the exact reproducer with the mandated GraalVM, and capture the complete output for inspection before editing.The full trace has no nested `Caused by:` entries. The actual failure is an inactive-condition error during eager test-class initialization: constructing the static `StorageSharedKeyCredential` triggers Azure Core’s reflective MethodHandle lookup before any of the five generated `com.azure.storage.blob` condition types has been reached. I’m checking the generated entries and test initialization order to fix that timing rather than adding unsupported behavior.The condition-order fix worked: execution advanced through initialization. The next complete trace again has no `Caused by:` entries and reports genuinely missing constructor-invocation metadata for `BlobStorageExceptionInternal`; cycle 1 collected that constructor under the already-reached `BlobsImpl` condition. I’ll merge that generated trace into the cycle-0 input, then rerun the exact reproducer.The rerun reused the old native executable (`nativeTraceImage UP-TO-DATE`), so it could not contain the merged constructor registration. I’ll remove only that coordinate’s stale native-image output and rerun the unchanged reproducer so the updated metadata input is actually compiled in.Implemented the fix in:\n\n- `tests/src/com.azure/azure-storage-blob/12.29.0/src/test/java/com_azure/azure_storage_blob/Azure_storage_blobTest.java`\n\nRoot cause: generated metadata for `BoundMethodHandle$Species_L` was inactive because `StorageSharedKeyCredential` initialized before `PublicAccessType` was reached. The full trace contained no `Caused by:` entries.\n\nFix: initialize and reuse `PublicAccessType.CONTAINER` before the credential, activating its metadata condition.\n\nValidation with the mandated GraalVM:\n\n- Exact reproducer: **8/8 tests passed**\n- Coordinate checkstyle: **passed**\n- `fissile check --staged`: **passed**\n"}], "isError": false, "timestamp": 1791822910460}}
